{
  "id": "COMPOUND:12871 - PROTEIN:1235",
  "verbalization": "SB-1578 is implicated in the regulation of Potassium channel subfamily K member 9 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that SB-1578 acts as a target of two different compounds, Piriferine and Khonklonginol F, both of which are cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. These inhibitors are known to modulate the activity of potassium channels, which are critical for cellular electrophysiology and are involved in various physiological processes, including neuronal function and cardiac rhythm. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to SB-1578 as a target of these inhibitors implies a potential role in the regulation of potassium channel activity, possibly through the inhibition of cyclin-dependent kinases that control channel expression or function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which SB-1578 influences potassium channel activity, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
